# 例外 · Findings accepted with a reason. Each line is a rule id; the
# comment above it says why it does not apply here.

# DS-0002 — "Specify at least 1 USER command in Dockerfile".
#
# `client/Dockerfile` deliberately has none: nginx's master process must
# start as root to bind privileged port 80, then drops its own workers
# to the unprivileged `nginx` user. `USER nginx` would break the bind.
# Containment comes from the compose contract instead — `cap_drop: ALL`
# with only CHOWN/SETUID/SETGID/NET_BIND_SERVICE added, a read-only root
# filesystem, and `no-new-privileges`. The Dockerfile carries the same
# note at the line the scanner points at.
#
# The server image is `FROM scratch` and runs as 65532:65532, so this
# exception covers exactly one file.
DS-0002
